te C: can make correct decisions quickly (decision quality), known to be 100% reliable (reliability), creates positive atmosphere with crew (cooperation), but difficulty communicating ideas (communication), regarded as egocentric (crew), not willing to further education (adaptability). So strong reliability and decision, but communication issues.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but regarded as arrogant (crew), relatively weak leadership (crew), also arrogant may affect communication. So mixed.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Candidate C seems strong reliability, decision, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be serious for cockpit. Candidate B has stress and conscientiousness but uncooperative. Candidate A has leadership but unorganized and criticism. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nProbably Candidate C is strongest overall despite communication issues? But communication is critical. Egocentric and difficulty communicating could be safety risk. Candidate B's uncooperative also risk. Candidate A's unorganized may affect reliability. Candidate D's arrogance and weak leadership also risk.\n\nWe need to argue. Maybe we can ask other panel members for more info on communication of Candidate C or D. But we can make an initial recommendation. Since we have no other input, we can propose Candidate C as provisional, noting concerns.\n\nThus public message: I propose Candidate C, because reliability and decision quality, crew atmosphere, but note communication concerns. Vote for Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
