rumpy and uncooperative. No info on reliability beyond conscientiousness, but seems reliable. Communication issues? Uncooperative suggests crew cooperation issues. Candidate A: leadership, anticipation, but unorganized, not good at criticism. Candidate D: responsibility, problem solving, concentration, but arrogant, weak leadership.\n\nGiven the new evidence, C seems strongest overall. As agent_1, we can agree with C, but perhaps note that we still need to discuss other candidates before final decision, per coverage rule. So we can say we still recommend C but propose we need to evaluate B's stress handling and cooperation, and D's leadership, etc. Provide a brief argument.\n\nThus public message: I agree with Agent 3, maintain recommendation for C, but note we still need to discuss other candidates to ensure coverage. Provide evidence: C's stress resilience and technical competence now confirmed. Also note concerns about communication and egocentric but think they are manageable.\n\nMetadata: vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
